@page "/docs/components/button-group"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.ButtonGroup
<PageTitle>Button Group - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Button Group</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="button-group" />
        </div>
        <p>Joins related buttons, inputs and select triggers into one segmented control: inner corners square off and neighboring borders merge into one. It renders with <code>role="group"</code> and is meant for actions. When the buttons carry an on or off state, use Toggle Group instead.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(ButtonGroupUsageExample)" />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Sizes"
          Description="Buttons of any size merge the same way. Keep a single size within each group."
          Example="typeof(ButtonGroupSizesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Vertical"
          Description="Set `Orientation` to `Vertical` to stack the segments, here as a pair of zoom controls."
          Example="typeof(ButtonGroupVerticalExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Split button"
          Description="A primary action next to a dropdown of alternatives. Place a `BzButtonGroupSeparator` between segments that share a filled variant so they stay visually distinct."
          Example="typeof(ButtonGroupSplitExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Text"
          Description="`BzButtonGroupText` is a static segment for a label, unit or prefix that sits flush with the buttons."
          Example="typeof(ButtonGroupTextExample)" />

    <Demo Title="With input"
          Description="An input works as a segment too. It stretches to fill the group while the button keeps its size."
          Example="typeof(ButtonGroupInputExample)" />

    <Demo Title="With select"
          Description="A select trigger and an input merge like any other segments, here forming a currency and amount row."
          Example="typeof(ButtonGroupSelectExample)" />

    <Demo Title="With popover"
          Description="The trailing segment opens a popover through `RenderAs`, which leaves room for richer content than a menu while the group still reads as one control."
          Example="typeof(ButtonGroupPopoverExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Nested"
          Description="Groups nested inside a group form one spaced cluster, and each inner group keeps its own merged edges."
          Example="typeof(ButtonGroupNestedExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL"
          Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, the segments run from right to left and the rounded outer corners move with them."
          Example="typeof(ButtonGroupRtlExample)" />
</div>
